---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Portrait from '../assets/nils-ingwersen.jpg';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="About Nils Ingwersen – full-stack software developer from Hamburg working with TypeScript, React, Next.js, maps, and AI."
		/>
		<style>
			.portrait {
				display: block;
				width: 160px;
				height: 160px;
				border-radius: 50%;
				box-shadow: var(--box-shadow);
			}
			.location {
				margin-top: -0.5em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
			}
			.entry {
				margin-bottom: 1.5em;
			}
			.entry h3 {
				margin-bottom: 0.25em;
			}
			.meta {
				margin: 0 0 0.5em 0;
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
			}
			dt {
				font-weight: 700;
				margin-top: 0.75em;
			}
			dd {
				margin-left: 0;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<Image class="portrait" src={Portrait} width={320} height={320} alt="Portrait of Nils Ingwersen" />
			<h1>About Me</h1>
			<p class="location">📍 Based in Hamburg, Germany</p>
			<p>
				I'm Nils, a software developer based in Hamburg with four years of experience building web
				products with TypeScript, React, and Next.js. I like working across the stack, especially on
				products involving maps, data, or AI.
			</p>

			<h2>Work Experience</h2>
			<div class="entry">
				<h3>Full-Stack Software Developer · Ubilabs, Hamburg</h3>
				<p class="meta">04/2024 – Present</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Build and ship web applications for different client products, mainly with React, TypeScript, and Next.js.</li>
					<li>Work with designers, project managers, developers, and client stakeholders from early concepts through production.</li>
					<li>Integrate APIs and AI features, implement server-side Next.js routes, and handle deployments on Google Cloud.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="entry">
				<h3>Full-Stack Developer · Boyens Media Group, Heide</h3>
				<p class="meta">07/2022 – 04/2024</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Built and maintained customer-facing web applications and internal tools across the full stack.</li>
					<li>Developed React and Next.js interfaces as well as PHP backend services and integrations.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<h2>Project Highlights</h2>
			<div class="entry">
				<h3>City Monitor for a Fire Department</h3>
				<p class="meta">Map frontend and real-time data</p>
				<p>
					Built the map frontend, data loading, and interactive MapLibre layers for a city-monitoring
					platform used daily by a fire department. Integrated DWD severe-weather data via
					WFS, WMS layers for precipitation and wind, polled live FlightAware data, and visualized river
					levels. Worked in a cross-functional team of five and supported the migration from Express and
					React to a consolidated Next.js application.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="entry">
				<h3>Google Maps – Maps Grounding Demo</h3>
				<p class="meta">Gemini integration and Google Cloud deployment</p>
				<p>
					Built most pages and all AI interactions for Google's public Maps Grounding demo, working
					directly with Google stakeholders in a cross-functional team. Integrated Gemini and Maps
					Grounding through Next.js API routes and built the tool execution layer that lets the agent
					control the map. A custom Gemini Live hook handles audio, sessions, and messages. Also owned
					deployment to Google Cloud Run using Cloud Build, Artifact Registry, and Cloud Storage.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>Skills</h2>
			<dl>
				<dt>Web</dt>
				<dd>React, TypeScript, Next.js, Zustand, TanStack Query, HTML, CSS</dd>
				<dt>Backend &amp; AI</dt>
				<dd>Node.js, Next.js API routes, REST APIs, Gemini SDK, LLM tool use</dd>
				<dt>Cloud &amp; Delivery</dt>
				<dd>Google Cloud, Cloud Run, Cloud Build, Artifact Registry, Cloud Storage, Docker, Terraform (basic)</dd>
				<dt>Maps &amp; Geospatial</dt>
				<dd>MapLibre, Mapbox, Google Maps, @vis.gl/react-google-maps, deck.gl</dd>
				<dt>Workflow &amp; Languages</dt>
				<dd>Git, code reviews, German (native), English</dd>
			</dl>

			<h2>Education</h2>
			<div class="entry">
				<h3>IT Specialist for Application Development · Boyens Media / Vocational Training Centre Dithmarschen</h3>
				<p class="meta">08/2019 – 07/2022</p>
				<p>Practice-oriented vocational training in professional software development, focused on web development, application logic, and data processing.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="entry">
				<h3>Applied Computer Science · Flensburg University of Applied Sciences</h3>
				<p class="meta">09/2016 – 02/2018</p>
				<p>Fundamentals of computer science, programming, and software development.</p>
			</div>

			<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nilsingwersen" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a></li>
				<li><a href="https://github.com/nilsingwersen" target="_blank">GitHub</a></li>
			</ul>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
